{"title":"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 27","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Remark_(Chinese_Remainder_Theorem)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Remark (Chinese Remainder Theorem)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(induction)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (induction)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(plain_recurrence_solving)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (plain recurrence solving)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the triangular array of numbers with 0,1,2,3,... along the sides and interior numbers obtained by adding the two adjacent numbers in the previous row. Rows 1 through 6 are shown.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/8/a88d2d1d58c16edbed53b60a92331b6918885af7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{tabular}{ccccccccccc} &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; 0 &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; 1 &amp; &amp; 1 &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ &amp; &amp; &amp; 2 &amp; &amp; 2 &amp; &amp; 2 &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ &amp; &amp; 3 &amp; &amp; 4 &amp; &amp; 4 &amp; &amp; 3 &amp; &amp; \\\\ &amp; 4 &amp; &amp; 7 &amp; &amp; 8 &amp; &amp; 7 &amp; &amp; 4 &amp; \\\\ 5 &amp; &amp; 11 &amp; &amp; 15 &amp; &amp; 15 &amp; &amp; 11 &amp; &amp; 5 \\end{tabular}\\]\" width=\"322\" height=\"110\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef0203e65664bd00b5f0325c5c5fcd81bcead8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> denote the sum of the numbers in row <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. What is the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/3/40396192d77313fb03786134c12eecfed6b5fd3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(100)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" /> is divided by 100?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/7/1f7eb87b74a7c0dd132d32d156f0c29515cafee3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ 12 } \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ 30 } \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ 50 } \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ 62 } \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ 74 }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"388\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that if we re-draw the table with an additional diagonal row on each side, the table is actually just two of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pascal%27s_Triangle\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Pascal&#39;s Triangle\">Pascal's Triangles</a>, except translated and summed. \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/a/75a013386ab29dc3b39bb75564c32da4ba4e1553.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{tabular}{ccccccccccccccc} &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; 1 &amp; &amp; 0 &amp; &amp; 1 &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; 1 &amp; &amp; 1 &amp; &amp; 1 &amp; &amp; 1 &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ &amp; &amp; &amp; 1 &amp; &amp; 2 &amp; &amp; 2 &amp; &amp; 2 &amp; &amp; 1 &amp; &amp; \\\\ &amp; &amp; 1 &amp; &amp; 3 &amp; &amp; 4 &amp; &amp; 4 &amp; &amp; 3 &amp; &amp; 1 &amp; \\\\ &amp; 1 &amp; &amp; 4 &amp; &amp; 7 &amp; &amp; 8 &amp; &amp; 7 &amp; &amp; 4 &amp; &amp; 1  \\\\ 1 &amp; &amp; 5 &amp; &amp; 11 &amp; &amp; 15 &amp; &amp; 15 &amp; &amp; 11 &amp; &amp; 5 &amp; &amp; 1 \\end{tabular}\\]\" width=\"434\" height=\"111\" />\n</p><p>The sum of a row of Pascal's triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/8/66877bd3ddd8dd7995544baee949cc4737866732.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"17\" />; the sum of two of each of these rows, subtracting away the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ones we included, yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/9/969ae6ab4138ed3be59d7f7791abd900270b45bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) = 2^n - 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"18\" />. Now, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/3/643296313844537776f7fb1c1df44d104a282144.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(100) = 2^{100} - 2 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"241\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3448749365c7d8391fbb54458b8a5dab2449ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(100) = 2^{100} - 2 \\equiv 2^{20 \\cdot 5} - 2 \\equiv -1 \\pmod{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"354\" height=\"19\" />, and by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Chinese_Remainder_Theorem\" title=\"Chinese Remainder Theorem\">Chinese Remainder Theorem</a>, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad2f10848b67192d1490146c58ecbb29214a5f86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(100) \\equiv 74 \\pmod{100} \\Longrightarrow \\mathrm{(E)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"253\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Remark_.28Chinese_Remainder_Theorem.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Remark_(Chinese_Remainder_Theorem)\">Remark (Chinese Remainder Theorem)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Remark (Chinese Remainder Theorem)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Solution 1 needs to calculate the last <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/6/4a62d9023875220ea7eb3a22159656b4986e1808.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{100}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />, meaning to solve <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/4/3045da7aafc18e407555c021467079896748dc01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{100} (\\bmod{ 100})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"110\" height=\"21\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/f/daf07ffd3dc98d2ecfcc3762bd42030ff47c7bb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100 = 4 \\cdot 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"94\" height=\"14\" />, we are going to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/a/56a42e680c6bec66c1e291e64c7031445f6f2fc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\bmod{ 100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/1/93148599dda3a9ee08de777c8603d25fab26a4d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\bmod{ 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"67\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/3/c73074bacc29fa67178ce8873e9aeac6fe285c89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\bmod{ 25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"76\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>By Chinese Remainder Theorem, the general solution of the system of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> linear congruences is:\n</p>\n<pre><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/3/5a33cf90f103de64ff6eb894efbb38aef5bf2277.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\equiv r_1 (\\bmod { \\quad m_1})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/5/f5553f1f91d52b592a23edf4871336a462586c35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\equiv r_2 (\\bmod { \\quad m_2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/2/942c227e3f1db997d4be45b2dc23707221bbfd14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(m_1, m_2) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"20\" />\nFind <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/2/7f2f57887b2e2f63a617b6a4b7a7d466c26c4342.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/7/cb72004e1c6c7b0782bbf2c7e40dcaad72993c4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/0/460c73dfa9b2d6bcd7c2e2453ffa6521ca2040f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_1 m_1 \\equiv 1 (\\bmod{ \\quad m_2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"167\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/d/f2d8192ffc01e71170b584d0adb047c360a4641a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_2 m_2 \\equiv 1 (\\bmod{ \\quad m_1})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"167\" height=\"20\" />\nThen <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/2/c927ef277d8295e125b86cdaa0326b99388d7bba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\equiv k_2 m_2 r_1 + k_1 m_1 r_2 (\\bmod{ \\quad m_1 m_2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"286\" height=\"20\" />\n</pre>\n<p>In this problem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/4/2a45a431123159391ed47bf1a3d7326a6b2fa174.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{100} \\equiv (2^{10})^{10} \\equiv 1024^{10} \\equiv 24^{10} \\equiv (-1)^{10} \\equiv 1 (\\bmod{ \\quad 25})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"433\" height=\"21\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/6/a0661e8adfd41a2b643d6d2392d4f0447020ed0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{100} \\equiv 0 (\\bmod{ \\quad 4})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"142\" height=\"21\" />:\n</p>\n<pre><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/8/508dee85a25b51078c3491f07b1f93a5d49ac67a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\equiv 1 (\\bmod{ \\quad 25})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"132\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/e/94e2f54476787c00f482a4c753f79ef251f04d6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\equiv 0 (\\bmod{ \\quad 4})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"123\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/7/637a522b42c74a244b5256a9fba3a766814a7ca5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(25, 4) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"85\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/a/f9abd700537ba9a4b4554d8c22cee9a07bdf8b46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\cdot 25 \\equiv 1 (\\bmod{ \\quad 4})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"152\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/3/4a36e2590757699596a909a64bdca7537cf98353.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19 \\cdot 4 \\equiv 1 (\\bmod{ \\quad 25})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"161\" height=\"20\" />\nThen <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/2/002815550433b9ae34becde9bda3f1d6125616e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\equiv 19 \\cdot 4 \\cdot 1 + 1 \\cdot 25 \\cdot 0 \\equiv 76 (\\bmod{ \\quad 100})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"322\" height=\"20\" />\n</pre>\n<p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Isabelchen\">isabelchen</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28induction.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(induction)\">Solution 2 (induction)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (induction)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We sum the first few rows: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/a/87a6cf875f0adcbece9c3866ffcef0d2a78c02a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0, 2, 6, 14, 30, 62$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"121\" height=\"16\" />. They are each two less than a power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so we try to prove it:\n</p><p>Let the sum of row <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/4/c74a070eea97d9363f58a257e05e75fc69efa753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"17\" />. To generate the next row, we add consecutive numbers. So we double the row, subtract twice the end numbers, then add twice the end numbers and add two. That makes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/4/9342f0f81be0301ecb7da567512b480439fe1a26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{n+1}=2S_n-2(n-1)+2(n-1)+2=2S_n+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"381\" height=\"18\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/4/c74a070eea97d9363f58a257e05e75fc69efa753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"17\" /> is two less than a power of 2, then it is in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/d/f8d327994a57c0251a274435a90a1c0e0d45efdd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^x-2$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/d/59d8977a854ffb025b93397b1d51a50c737563e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{n+1}=2^{x+1}-4+2=2^{x+1}-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"247\" height=\"19\" />. \n</p><p>Since the first row is two less than a power of 2, all the rest are. Since the sum of the elements of row 1 is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/a/5ea54c4506b33e97d66d0e33e43dd582ec3e3240.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^1-2$\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" />, the sum of the numbers in row <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/d/d6da5c1454acc95a15cb740792c300b0a98f2894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n-2$\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" />. Thus, using <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Modular_arithmetic\" title=\"Modular arithmetic\">Modular arithmetic</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/2/a22efc2688a06d0a864702cd732387ce0ff5818a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(100)=2^{100}-2 \\bmod{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"212\" height=\"21\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/8/50811f350197d47b2ddb684f3b7d07ce96a0bdca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{10}=1024$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"83\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/5/9f5f4a7a3e14cf775103c552bbce164f6187bce3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{100}-2\\equiv 24^{10}-2\\equiv (2^3 \\cdot 3)^{10} - 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"271\" height=\"19\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8132873ac63eaab99918f4c19d904724167185f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\equiv 1024^3 \\cdot 81 \\cdot 81 \\cdot 9 - 2 \\equiv 24^3 \\cdot 19^2 \\cdot 9 - 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"320\" height=\"15\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/e/89e22774247ee5639a1206aeb1496b6e94e2a8b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\equiv 74\\bmod{100} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{(E)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"163\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28plain_recurrence_solving.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(plain_recurrence_solving)\">Solution 3 (plain recurrence solving)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (plain recurrence solving)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We derive the recurrence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/e/60ee07ed4de13629f34716a206fa11062c9e196b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{n+1}=2S_n + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"121\" height=\"16\" /> as above. Without guessing the form of the solution at this point we can easily solve this recurrence. Note that one can easily get rid of the \"<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/5/fe54585e0c171194b0e07cc59767d097999658cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" />\" as follows: Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c127f81d2aa3922281902b4927ad430db899e888.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_n=T_n-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"15\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/0/b90227e59e90d572e6917600c65265956112e1a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{n+1}=T_{n+1}-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"128\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/e/0eeb19b3c2d73cc0e0ec6b7a1094c0545aac6234.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2S_n+2 = 2(T_n-2)+2 = 2T_n-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"274\" height=\"18\" />. Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/9/6f93d5452b9da4b4720c1f05c882edc46035bcd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_{n+1}=2T_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"16\" />. This obviously solves to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/1/dc198852377d5777322ab34737ff3d28d7f86c56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_n=2^{n-1} T_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"17\" />. As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/4/d04ec99b2c4eea758b597f943540b267cb6d1c7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_1=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/f/03f5d7d79b8cf385779515b44e74f2a23c31f88a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_1=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />. Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/d/cfd518c51b2e7af75ebe29f4a7aa1659a201608f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_n=2^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"61\" height=\"15\" /> and consecutively <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/0/30067b4c62128cd14b368e59748a7ab39973ebf4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_n=2^n-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"93\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME\" title=\"1995 AHSME\">1995 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1995 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1995\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 26\">Problem 26</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 28\">Problem 28</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems